THUMB-1 ASSEMBLY EXAMPLES

1. Exit cleanly with status 0 (source file /tmp/demo.s)
  movs r0, #3
  movs r1, #0
  svc #0

Run:
  as /tmp/demo.s
  /tmp/a.out
The interpreter inserts no implicit function prologue here.
For syscall numbers consult include/piconix_syscall.h.

2. Write one character to stdout and exit
  movs r0, #9
  movs r1, #1
  adr r2, msg
  movs r3, #2
  svc #0
  movs r0, #3
  movs r1, #0
  svc #0
  .align 2
  msg:
  .ascii "A\n"

Syscall 9 (write) uses fd in r1, buffer in r2, size in r3.
The 'adr' target must be forward, aligned and in range.
Use only listed mnemonics/directives; do not paste GNU as code.

3. Inspect generated assembly from cc
  cc /tmp/demo.c
  cat /tmp/demo.s
  as /tmp/demo.s

Source and output are RAM-limited. Branches are range-limited.
If assembler rejects a label, shorten code or adjust placement.
